# The bitten (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "The bitten, the clock and what you carry"). [Bitten] topics show only
# while the HUD shows a bite. Telling a safehouse is its own built service; nothing here reads whether
# a cleaned bite took. Saying you're not bitten while it shows is a lie, and its tell is the symptoms.

conv occupant.bitten.declare
for occupant
when bite_shown & !declared
topic "[Bitten] I need to tell you something."
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say "Show me, then. Roll the sleeve up. Nobody here is going to shout, and nobody's going to reach for a gun. That's the rule in every Haven house: say it out loud, and we help if we can."
  > @tell "Here. It's a bite." -> told   do call:declare_bite
  > @fine "It's nothing. A scratch off a fence." -> fine | caught   check lie haven 2   truth !bite_shown   found nset:hid_bite
  > @back "Not now. I'm not ready to say it." -> hub

node told
  say "Thank you for saying it out loud. Most don't. The medic will look at it, and it goes in the book, so nobody finds out the hard way. Sit by the door where it's cooler, and drink something."
  say "If it's young, Halcyon's lab gives a trial dose, once, to anyone bitten. It's a long walk and a short form. We'll talk about that when you've sat down."
  > @back1 "Thank you. Can I ask something else?" -> hub

node fine
  say "A fence. Right. Keep it covered, then, and keep it clean. And if it goes hot and you start sweating in the cold, you come back to this door and say the other word. We'll still open it."
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node caught
  say "That's not a fence. I've seen enough of them now to know the shape of the teeth. I'm writing it down, at least, so the medic knows what's walking round this house."
  do call:caught_bite
  > @tell2 "All right. It's a bite. Write it down." -> told   do call:declare_bite
  > @back3 "Leave it. Please." -> hub

conv occupant.bitten.found
for occupant
when nmem:hid_bite
greet
prio reaction
once
voice haven

node start
  say? nmem:hid_bite :: "You told us it was a fence. It wasn't. We worked it out after you'd gone. Next time say it at the door. We'd have helped. That's the whole point of having a door."

conv halcyon.bitten.trial
for leader:halcyon, named:halcyon
when bite_shown
topic "[Bitten] Tell me about the trial dose."
prio quest
voice halcyon

node start
  say "There is a trial dose. Anyone bitten may volunteer for it, once, at no cost. It is a trial. We record everything about it, including you."
  say "Eight in ten volunteers walk out. Ask at the table by the lab gate, and bring the bite while it's young. Older bites are less interesting to us, and less hopeful for you."
  > @consent "What would I have to sign?" -> sign
  > @back "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node sign
  say "Your name, the time of the bite, and your consent. The form is short. We are told that is a kindness. The other two in ten are written up as carefully as the eight. More carefully, if anything."
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.doctor.symptoms
for wanderer:doctor
when !bite_shown & stage:fever
topic "[Fever] What's wrong with me?"
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say "Look at me. Eyes. Now your hands, palms up. That isn't a bite. That's a fever, and an ordinary one, probably. People still get those. The world ending didn't cure the flu."
  say "Water, rest, and stop running everywhere. If it's still on you tomorrow, find a Haven house with a medic. They'll see you for nothing. They see everyone for nothing."
  > @sure "Only probably?" -> probably
  > @back "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node probably
  say "Everything's probably now. I haven't got a lab or a second opinion, I've got a bag and my eyes. Probably is the best word we've got left, and I don't use it lightly."
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv occupant.nurse.symptoms
for occupant
when house:short & bg:nurse,doctor
topic "[Nurse] Who's that coughing?"
prio world
voice haven

node start
  say "The little one at the back. She's been coughing since the school trip, since before all this, and now people move their bowls away from her at supper."
  say (her father) "It's her chest. It's always been her chest. I keep telling them, and they look at me like I'd say anything."
  say "People look at her like she's bitten. She isn't. Is she? You'd know. You've the hands for it."
  > @chest "That isn't a bite. It's her chest." -> chest   if bg:nurse,doctor
  > @back "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node chest
  say "Say it again, louder, at supper. They'll listen to you. They don't listen to him, because he's her father, and everybody knows a father would say anything."
  do learn:house.cough@here
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub
